        "title": "Simplifying a Rational Expression Using the Pythagorean Identity"
      },
      "question": {
        ":question/id": "f206d2c2-ee8e-56e4-8de0-ea23491335cf",
        ":question/problem": "$\\frac{{sin}^{3}\u2061x{cos}^{2}\u2061x+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x{cos}^{4}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}=$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First, we factor the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{sin}^{3}\u2061x{cos}^{2}\u2061x+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x{cos}^{4}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x{cos}^{2}\u2061x({sin}^{2}\u2061x+{cos}^{2}\u2061x)}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nNext, we use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, and then we simplify the resulting expression as much as possible.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x{cos}^{2}\u2061x({sin}^{2}\u2061x+{cos}^{2}\u2061x)}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x{cos}^{2}\u2061x\\cdot 1}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x{cos}^{2}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}\\cdot \\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}{1} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{sin}^{3}\u2061x{cos}^{2}\u2061x+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x{cos}^{4}\u2061x}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x.\n$$",
