      "question": {
        ":question/id": "408e1d81-b8ca-526c-9d23-4441a1e9e3da",
        ":question/problem": "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t{cos}^{2}\u2061t+{sin}^{3}\u2061t}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t}.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First, we factor the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t{cos}^{2}\u2061t+{sin}^{3}\u2061t}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t}=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t\\cdot ({cos}^{2}\u2061t+{sin}^{2}\u2061t)}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, and then we simplify the resulting expression as much as possible.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t\\cdot ({cos}^{2}\u2061t+{sin}^{2}\u2061t)}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t\\cdot 1}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}\u2061t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t{cos}^{2}\u2061t+{sin}^{3}\u2061t}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t}=\\operatorname{tan}\u2061t.\n$$",
